# Text and Paragraph: the same text box with two roles, and a For element: Paragraph rule that reaches only paragraphs.
Document (dev.stxt.pdf):
	Language: en
	Title: Text and Paragraph · Text or Paragraph
	Page:
		Paper: A4
		Margin: 20mm
	Styles:
		For element: Paragraph
			Typography:
				Font: IBM Plex Serif
				Size: 11
				Line height: 16
				Align: justify
	Section:
		Text: Text and Paragraph
			Style: topic
		Heading 1:
			Text: Text or Paragraph
		Paragraph: A `Paragraph` is a paragraph of the content and a `Text` is standalone text: a label, a figure, a line of a header. Both break their text into lines. Here a `For element: Paragraph` rule gives the paragraphs a serif font and justified lines, and the texts keep the base typography.
			Style: intro
			Typography:
				Font: IBM Plex Sans
				Size: 10
				Line height: 14
				Align: left
		Text: Text: Madrid, 3 March 2026
			Style: label
		Text: Madrid, 3 March 2026
			Box:
				Margin: 0 0 14 0
		Text: Paragraph: Dear Ms. García, ...
			Style: label
		Paragraph: Dear Ms. García,
		Paragraph: We confirm the order of twelve walnut chairs, which will be delivered in two weeks to the address given in the order, together with the invoice and the care instructions for the oil finish.
